WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:04.270
Pour one out for Game of Thrones, because
winter has finally come for the most popular

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:06.310
TV show in recent history.

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:09.930
But before you start crying over the fate
of your beloved characters, remember that

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:12.300
for the show's actors, there's life after
death.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:15.710
Here's a look at what the stars behind these
dead Game of Thrones characters look like

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:16.200
today.

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:20.740
Ros went from being a Northern prostitute
to Littlefinger's trusted assistant at one

00:00:20.741 --> 00:00:25.350
of his King's Landing brothels, but her increased
station came with a price—Littlefinger discovered

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:28.360
that she was spying on him for Varys, so he
gave her to Joffrey.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:32.230
It all ended quite brutally for Ros, who was
bound to Joffrey's bed frame and killed with

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:34.410
several crossbow bolts in season three.

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:39.260
Since her gruesome Thrones demise, actress
Esmé Bianco has appeared in the TV movies

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:43.470
A Christmas Mystery and Ominous, as well as
the television series The Magicians.

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:48.030
Her recent film projects include Hypnotized,
about people trapped under hypnosis when their

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:52.020
hypnotist falls into a coma, and the found-footage
vampire thriller Living Among Us.

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:57.040
The "Red Viper" Oberyn Martell traveled to
King's Landing in hopes of finding answers

00:00:57.059 --> 00:00:59.100
regarding the death of his sister Elia.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:02.480
Oberyn got more than he bargained for when
he volunteered to fight for Tyrion during

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:07.080
a trial by combat against Gregor in season
four; he got the answer he wanted, but Gregor

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:09.850
smashed his face like a grape not long after.

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:14.830
Since Thrones, actor Pedro Pascal has starred
in Graceland, Narcos, The Great Wall, and

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:16.240
Kingsman: The Golden Circle.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.280
His star power is only continuing to rise
as he prepares to take the title role in the

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:25.280
Disney+ Star Wars series The Mandalorian and
an as-yet unidentified part in Wonder Woman

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:26.280
1984.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:31.920
The "kissed-by-fire" wildling Ygritte, played
by Rose Leslie, entered into a passionate

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:33.900
romance with Jon Snow, but it wasn't meant
to be.

00:01:33.910 --> 00:01:37.820
Jon abandoned her and was later forced to
watch her struck down in the season four battle

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:38.820
between their forces.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:40.440
She was ultimately killed by someone else's
arrow, but her death weighed heavy on Jon.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:41.900
You know nothing, Jon Snow."

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:46.570
Leslie has kept busy since leaving Game of
Thrones, continuing her role in Downton Abbey

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:48.650
and starring in The Last Witch Hunter.

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:53.000
Leslie and Thrones co-star Kit Harington also
became romantically involved after she left

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:56.030
the series, culminating in their summer 2018
wedding.

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:59.780
Her recent projects include a main role in
the CBS legal drama The Good Fight.

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:04.580
Barristan Selmy made his way across the sea
to join Daenerys Targaryen as one of her closest

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:05.640
advisors.

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:09.880
During their time in Meereen, the elusive
Sons of the Harpy lay an ambush for the Unsullied

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:12.600
in season five, killing many before Ser Barristan
arrived.

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:17.900
He took out nearly a dozen enemies single-handedly
saving grey Worm, but died in the effort.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:22.060
Despite being upset about Barristan's early
demise, star Ian McElhinney has moved on with

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:26.640
his career, appearing in Derry Girls, Rebellion,
and Rogue One: A Star Wars Story.

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:30.760
He can currently be seen as scientist Val-El
on Syfy's Superman series Krypton.

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:36.000
Stannis' daughter Shireen had royal blood
— which is why Melisandre insisted on bringing

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:39.019
the child with them when Stannis' army marched
to Winterfell.

00:02:39.019 --> 00:02:42.779
Unfortunately, Shireen didn't live to see
the end of that march; she was sacrificed

00:02:42.779 --> 00:02:46.879
by the Red Priestess in season five, when
Melisandre convinced Stannis and his wife

00:02:46.879 --> 00:02:50.459
to let her burn Shireen at the stake for a
blessing from the Lord of Light.

00:02:50.459 --> 00:02:54.559
After her character's horrible fate on Game
of Thrones, young actress Kerry Ingram moved

00:02:54.559 --> 00:02:56.290
on to other television roles.

00:02:56.290 --> 00:03:00.699
She's appeared in the shows Wolf Hall, Doctors,
and Barbarians Rising, and can currently be

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:03.220
seen in the Netflix original series Free Rein.

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:07.709
Stannis sacrificed his daughter to gain the
blessing of the Lord of Light, but blessings

00:03:07.709 --> 00:03:11.579
weren't exactly what he received in return:
his wife took her own life, half of his army

00:03:11.579 --> 00:03:14.209
deserted him, and all of his horses were stolen.

00:03:14.209 --> 00:03:18.199
The remnants of his forces were easily swept
away by the Bolton army, and the defeated

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:20.740
Stannis was killed by Brienne during the season
five finale.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:25.809
Since Game of Thrones, actor Stephen Dillane
has appeared on the television show The Tunnel

00:03:25.809 --> 00:03:27.699
and in films like Mary Shelley.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:32.120
And he also made an appearance on this hit
Netflix biographical series The Crown as well.

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:36.800
As the youngest Stark child, Rickon didn't
get a lot of screen time before he and Osha

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:39.549
separated from Bran's group in season three.

00:03:39.549 --> 00:03:43.620
They reappeared in season six as captives
of Ramsay Bolton, and during the Battle of

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:47.860
the Bastards, Ramsay set Rickon free, telling
him to run to Jon Snow before firing on the

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:48.360
boy.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:51.440
He nearly made it, but one of Ramsay's arrows
struck, killing Rickon.

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:56.640
Art Parkinson has scored several roles since
leaving Thrones, including his 2016 stint

00:03:56.650 --> 00:04:00.829
voicing the title role in the animated film
Kubo and the Two Strings and an appearance

00:04:00.829 --> 00:04:01.950
in the movie Zoo.

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:05.500
He can currently be seen on the U.K. police
procedural series The Bay.

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:10.420
Beginning in season three, Ramsay Bolton shocked
Game of Thrones fans with his cruelty on a

00:04:10.439 --> 00:04:14.949
regular basis—and eventually, as viewers
knew it would, it all caught up with him.

00:04:14.949 --> 00:04:18.609
Following Ramsay's defeat at the Battle of
the Bastards in season six, it looked like

00:04:18.609 --> 00:04:22.789
Jon Snow might beat him to death—but he
held off, giving the honors to his sister

00:04:22.789 --> 00:04:26.640
Sansa, who made use of the loyal dogs Ramsay
had been starving for seven days.

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:30.500
Given the chance to take a bite of their master's
bloody face, they tucked right in.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:34.900
Iwan Rheon's stock has soared since Thrones;
he's appeared in several shows, including

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:37.330
as Maximus in the Marvel series Inhumans.

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:42.480
In 2019, he appeared in Netflix's Mötley
Crüe biopic The Dirt as guitarist Mick Mars.

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:47.560
The politically savvy and whip-smart Margaery
Tyrell nearly managed to resolve her family's

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:48.440
issues with the Faith.

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:52.460
Unfortunately, no one heeded her warnings
about the lengths Cersei would go in order

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:54.000
to "protect" her son.

00:04:54.009 --> 00:04:58.470
"Cersei understands the consequences of her
absence, and yet she is absent anyway, which

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:00.481
means she does not intend to suffer those
consequences.

00:05:00.481 --> 00:05:01.950
The trial can wait.

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:04.200
We all need to leave."

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:08.740
In a pivotal scene from the season six finale,
Margaery and much of her family — along

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:13.919
with the High Sparrow — were consumed alive
by Wildfire after Cersei put her plan in motion.

00:05:13.919 --> 00:05:18.430
Recently, actress Natalie Dormer lent her
voice to the 2017 game Mass Effect: Andromeda

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:22.840
and appeared in the miniseries Picnic at Hanging
Rock and the films In Darkness and Patient

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:23.340
Zero.

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:27.680
Next, she'll be seen in the Penny Dreadful
spin-off City of Angels and heard in The Dark

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:32.420
Crystal: Age of Resistance, Netflix's prequel
to Jim Henson's fantasy classic.

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:37.080
Tommen Baratheon became an unlikely king when
he succeeded to the throne after Joffrey died

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:37.920
at the "Purple Wedding."

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:42.030
After witnessing his mother blow up the Sept
of Baelor — killing his wife and all others

00:05:42.030 --> 00:05:46.140
inside — Tommen jumped from a balcony in
the Red Keep during the season six finale.

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:50.280
Since departing Game of Thrones, young star
Dean Charles Chapman has booked roles in the

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:55.180
films Breathe and The Commuter, as well as
a regular role on AMC's Into the Badlands.

00:05:55.780 --> 00:06:00.160
Dame Diana Rigg was already an acting legend
thanks to roles in films like On Her Majesty's

00:06:00.169 --> 00:06:04.419
Secret Service and TV series like The Avengers
when she arrived on Game of Thrones, but she

00:06:04.419 --> 00:06:08.419
quickly carved out yet another legendary role
for herself as the witty and dangerous Queen

00:06:08.419 --> 00:06:10.509
of Thorns, Lady Olenna Tyrell.

00:06:10.509 --> 00:06:14.340
When she finally met her end in the season
7 episode "The Queen's Justice," she was the

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:18.240
last remaining major player in her house and
she'd already done plenty of damage to the

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:18.740
Lannisters.

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:23.040
As Jaime Lannister forced her to drink poison
rather than be tortured, she dealt one last

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:26.680
blow and admitted she was the one who poisoned
his son Joffrey at his own wedding.

00:06:27.229 --> 00:06:28.760
"Tell Cersei.

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:34.930
I want her to know it was me."

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:39.300
Since exiting Thrones, Rigg has continued
to act, most recently as the Duchess of Buccleuch

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:41.870
in the hit TV series Victoria.

00:06:41.870 --> 00:06:45.780
Aidan Gillen's Littlefinger remained among
Game of Thrones' longest-serving and most

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:50.240
frustratingly capable survivors right up until
the end of season 7, when one of the great

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:52.639
schemers in Westeros finally met his end.

00:06:52.639 --> 00:06:57.280
He seized power in the Eyrie, won favor with
Sansa Stark, and then very nearly managed

00:06:57.280 --> 00:07:01.550
to turn the Stark children against each other
when they were all finally reunited at Winterfell.

00:07:01.550 --> 00:07:05.610
Then, at long last, Arya and Sansa revealed
that they had Littlefinger right where they

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:08.400
wanted him, and Arya executed him with his
own dagger.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:12.409
It was one of the show's most satisfying deaths,
and the end of one of the show's most persistent

00:07:12.409 --> 00:07:13.409
villains.

00:07:13.409 --> 00:07:17.270
"Thank you for all your lessons, Lord Baelish.

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:19.970
I will never forget them."

00:07:19.970 --> 00:07:23.770
Gillen's been in high demand ever since his
work in the days of The Wire, and that hasn't

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:25.440
changed since he left Thrones.

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:29.479
As he was ending his time on that series,
he joined the acclaimed series Peaky Blinders,

00:07:29.479 --> 00:07:33.650
played a role in Bohemian Rhapsody, and continued
his work in The Maze Runner franchise.

00:07:33.650 --> 00:07:38.389
In January 2019 his new series Project Blue
Book, about the U.S. government's hunt for

00:07:38.389 --> 00:07:40.979
UFOs, premiered on the History Channel.

00:07:40.979 --> 00:07:45.510
Nymeria Sand was one of the three Sand Snakes
who helped Ellaria Sand seize and hold power

00:07:45.510 --> 00:07:48.479
in Dorne after the death of her father, Oberyn
Martell.

00:07:48.479 --> 00:07:52.379
Unfortunately for her, she and her sister
Obara were abruptly killed at the violent

00:07:52.379 --> 00:07:53.680
hands of Euron Greyjoy.

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:58.440
The last time we see Nymeria, she's strung
up by her own whip on the bow of Euron's ship.

00:07:58.440 --> 00:08:02.160
Star Jessica Henwick has only become more
prominent since her character's death, though.

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:06.610
In 2017, as her time on Thrones was ending,
she started playing martial artist and teacher

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:09.460
Colleen Wing on the Netflix series Iron Fist.

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:13.879
She also appeared as Colleen in a cameo appearance
in the second season of Luke Cage, and played

00:08:13.879 --> 00:08:16.210
a major role in the crossover event The Defenders.

00:08:16.210 --> 00:08:20.930
Her next major franchise project is a role
in Godzilla vs. Kong, scheduled to be released

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:21.620
in 2020.

00:08:22.449 --> 00:08:26.540
Benjen Stark has one of the more interesting
arcs in the course of Game of Thrones' run.

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:30.249
After appearing early in the first season
and welcoming his nephew Jon to the Night's

00:08:30.249 --> 00:08:34.750
Watch, Benjen ventures out beyond the Wall
and isn't heard from again until season 6,

00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:39.060
when he reveals to his nephew Bran and Meera
Reed that he's now undead, having been stabbed

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:42.919
by the White Walkers and then brought back
from the brink by the Children of the Forest.

00:08:42.919 --> 00:08:46.600
He was never fully converted into a wight,
which means he can fight for the living, but

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:50.381
he's too far gone to cross back over the Wall
and pass through its many enchantments, so

00:08:50.381 --> 00:08:52.370
he does what he can from the far North.

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:56.970
In season 7, that includes sacrificing himself
to the wights to save Jon, ending his watch

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:58.080
once and for all.

00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:02.320
Outside of Game of Thrones, actor Joseph Mawle's
career continues to gain traction.

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:07.260
He was cast as Odysseus in in the 2018 TV
series Troy: Fall of a City; he can also be

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:11.850
seen as George Orwell in the biographical
drama Mr. Jones, and alongside Richard Gere

00:09:11.850 --> 00:09:14.100
in the British drama series MotherFatherSon.

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:18.940
The middle seasons of Game of Thrones told,
among other things, the story of the North's

00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:23.550
disintegration into chaos, as the largest
of the seven kingdoms shifted from steadfast

00:09:23.550 --> 00:09:27.110
bastion of honor and durability to a Bolton-led
mess.

00:09:27.110 --> 00:09:31.130
When Jon and Sansa finally started putting
the North back together under Stark banners,

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:35.529
they met Lyanna Mormont, the pint-sized Lady
of Bear Island, who ultimately proved to be

00:09:35.529 --> 00:09:38.740
one of the most effective and unflinching
leaders the show has ever seen.

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:42.680
In her final days, Lyanna refused to hide
from the fight against the dead, opting to

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:46.920
lead her men rather than take shelter from
the battle, and she went down like a boss,

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:49.340
stabbing an undead giant in the eye as he
crushed her.

00:09:49.340 --> 00:09:53.040
Game of Thrones was the world's introduction
to young Bella Ramsey, and her acting career

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:56.910
has steadily gained momentum ever since her
debut on the show in 2016.

00:09:56.910 --> 00:10:01.720
Her other credits now include the title roles
in the TV series Hilda and The Worst Witch,

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:06.380
and this year she'll also co-star in two period
drama films, the Judy Garland biopic Judy

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:08.660
and the World War II drama Resistance.

00:10:09.130 --> 00:10:11.320
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:10:11.320 --> 00:10:14.940
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
stars are coming soon.

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:18.800
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

